[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Clean Architecture and Separation of Concerns in Android"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Clean Architecture helps developers build robust, maintainable, and testable Android applications. By enforcing strict boundaries between different parts of the codebase, we achieve a true Separation of Concerns (SoC)."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"The Core Layers"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"A standard Clean Architecture implementation in Android typically consists of three distinct layers: Presentation, Domain, and Data."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Presentation Layer: Contains UI components like Activities, Fragments, and ViewModels. It deals with rendering state and capturing user input."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Domain Layer: The heart of the application. It contains business logic, UseCases (Interactors), and domain models. It is completely independent of Android framework APIs."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Data Layer: Responsible for fetching data from local databases, network APIs, or cache. It implements repositories defined in the Domain layer."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing the Domain Layer"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"The Domain layer should be pure Kotlin with no dependencies on Android frameworks. Here is an example of a UseCase implementation."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"class GetUserProfileUseCase(private val userRepository: UserRepository) {
    suspend operator fun invoke(userId: String): Result<User> {
        return userRepository.getUser(userId)
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Implementing the Presentation Layer"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The ViewModel interacts with the UseCase to fetch data and exposes it to the UI via StateFlow or LiveData."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"class ProfileViewModel(private val getUserProfileUseCase: GetUserProfileUseCase) : ViewModel() {
    private val _uiState = MutableStateFlow<ProfileUiState>(ProfileUiState.Loading)
    val uiState: StateFlow<ProfileUiState> = _uiState.asStateFlow()

    fun loadProfile(userId: String) {
        viewModelScope.launch {
            val result = getUserProfileUseCase(userId)
            _uiState.value = if (result.isSuccess) {
                ProfileUiState.Success(result.getOrThrow())
            } else {
                ProfileUiState.Error("Failed to load profile")
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":14,"type":"heading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Separation of concerns via Clean Architecture ensures that changes in the UI or database do not ripple through the entire codebase. This makes writing unit tests straightforward and keeps your application scalable."}]
